01:02:13,333 --> 01:02:19,333
Johnny Got His Gun is a 1971 American independent anti-war
drama film written and directed by Dalton Trumbo.

11
01:08:26,666 --> 01:08:32,666
Based on his own novel of the same name, it was
Trumbo's first and only directorial effort.

12
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
The film stars Timothy Bottoms, Kathy Fields, Marsha Hunt,
Jason Robards, Donald Sutherland, and Diane Varsi.

13
01:20:53,333 --> 01:20:59,333
Although it was a minor success upon its initial release, the film
was largely forgotten by the mass audience soon after.

14
01:27:06,666 --> 01:27:12,666
It received renewed attention in the late 1980s after clips from it were incorporated into the popular
music video for Metallica's single "One", and the film has subsequently become a cult film.

15
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
Eventually, Metallica bought the rights to the film in order to be able to
show the music video without having to keep paying royalties.

16
01:39:33,333 --> 01:39:39,333
The film explores themes of blindness and impaired vision,
experiment, amputation, world war i, deaf-mute.

17
01:45:46,666 --> 01:45:52,666
The tone is emotional.
